WeylAlgebras -- algorithms for D-modules
****************************************

Description
===========

To begin, read the *note D-modules tutorial: (Dmodules)D-modules tutorial,.

How to make Weyl algebras

  * *note monoid(...,WeylAlgebra=>...):
    (Macaulay2Doc)monoid_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmWeylAlgebra=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, -- specify
    differential operators in the ring
  * *note makeWeylAlgebra: makeWeylAlgebra, -- Weyl algebra corresponding to a
    polynomial ring

Basic commands

  * *note gbw: gbw, -- compute a Gröbner basis with respect to a weight vector
  * *note inw: inw, -- get the initial term or ideal with respect to a weight
    vector
  * *note Fourier: Fourier, -- Fourier transform for Weyl algebra
  * *note Dtransposition: Dtransposition, -- standard transposition for Weyl
    algebra
  * *note stafford: stafford, -- computes 2 generators for a given ideal in the
    Weyl algebra
  * *note makeCyclic: makeCyclic, -- finds a cyclic generator of a D-module
  * *note Dprune: Dprune, -- prunes a D-module

Basic invariants of D-modules

  * *note Ddim: Ddim, -- dimension of a D-module
  * *note isHolonomic: isHolonomic, -- determines whether a D-module (or ideal
    in Weyl algebra) is holonomic
  * *note holonomicRank: holonomicRank, -- holonomic rank of a D-module
  * *note characteristicIdeal: characteristicIdeal, -- characteristic ideal of
    a D-module
  * *note DsingularLocus: DsingularLocus, -- singular locus of a D-module

Programming aids

  * *note createDpairs: createDpairs, -- pairs coordinate and derivation
    variables in a Weyl algebra
  * *note extractDiffsAlgebra: extractDiffsAlgebra, -- underlying polynomial
    ring in the differentials of a Weyl algebra
  * *note extractVarsAlgebra: extractVarsAlgebra, -- underlying polynomial ring
    in the ordinary variables of a Weyl algebra
  * *note Dtrace: Dtrace, -- set or get the depth of comments made by D-module
    routines
* Menu:

* makeWeylAlgebra::             Weyl algebra corresponding to a polynomial ring
* gbw::                         compute a Gröbner basis with respect to a weight vector
* inw::                         get the initial term or ideal with respect to a weight vector
* Fourier::                     Fourier transform for Weyl algebra
