makeWeylAlgebra -- Weyl algebra corresponding to a polynomial ring
******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        makeWeylAlgebra R
        makeWA R
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note polynomial ring: (Macaulay2Doc)PolynomialRing,, the
        (commutative) polynomial ring
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * SetVariables => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default
        value true, indicates whether the generators should be assigned to
        global variables
  * Outputs:
      * a *note polynomial ring: (Macaulay2Doc)PolynomialRing,, the
        (non-commutative) Weyl algebra

Description
===========

Given a polynomial ring R with variables x_1,..,x_n, this routine returns a
Weyl algebra with variables x_1,..,x_n and dx_1,..,dx_n.

+-----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,z]                             |
|                                               |
|o1 = R                                         |
|                                               |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                            |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : D = makeWeylAlgebra R                     |
|                                               |
|o2 = D                                         |
|                                               |
|o2 : PolynomialRing, 3 differential variable(s)|
+-----------------------------------------------+

To skip naming the ring, use parentheses.

+-----------------------------------------------+
|i3 : makeWA(QQ[x,y,z])                         |
|                                               |
|o3 = QQ[x..z, dx, dy, dz]                      |
|                                               |
|o3 : PolynomialRing, 3 differential variable(s)|
+-----------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

The polynomial ring R must be commutative.

See also
========

  * *note monoid(...,WeylAlgebra=>...):
    (Macaulay2Doc)monoid_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmWeylAlgebra=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, -- specify
    differential operators in the ring
* Menu:

* createDpairs::                pairs coordinate and derivation variables in a Weyl algebra
* extractDiffsAlgebra::         underlying polynomial ring in the differentials of a Weyl algebra
* extractVarsAlgebra::          underlying polynomial ring in the ordinary variables of a Weyl algebra

Ways to use makeWeylAlgebra:
============================

  * "makeWeylAlgebra(PolynomialRing)"

