Dtransposition -- standard transposition for Weyl algebra
*********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        Dtransposition A
  * Inputs:
      * A, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, a matrix (between free
        modules), function, ideal, or chain complex of free modules over the
        Weyl algebra
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, the standard transpose of A as a
        matrix, function, ideal, or chain complex over the Weyl algebra

Description
===========

                                                                            
The standard transposition is the involution of the Weyl algebra which sends
 a b        b a
x d  to (-d) x . It provides the equivalence in the Weyl algebra between left
and right D-modules.

+-----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : makeWeylAlgebra(QQ[x,y])                  |
|                                               |
|o1 = QQ[x..y, dx, dy]                          |
|                                               |
|o1 : PolynomialRing, 2 differential variable(s)|
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : L = x^2*dy + y*dy^2 + 3*dx^5*dy           |
|                                               |
|        5      2         2                     |
|o2 = 3dx dy + x dy + y*dy                      |
|                                               |
|o2 : QQ[x..y, dx, dy]                          |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i3 : Dtransposition L                          |
|                                               |
|        5      2         2                     |
|o3 = 3dx dy - x dy + y*dy  + 2dy               |
|                                               |
|o3 : QQ[x..y, dx, dy]                          |
+-----------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

The standard transposition of a left ideal should be a right ideal, however M2
currently doesn't support right modules. Thus the output is left ideal
generated by the transposition of the previous generators.

See also
========

  * *note WeylAlgebra: (Macaulay2Doc)monoid_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmWeylAlgebra=>_pd_pd_
    pd_rp, -- specify differential operators in the ring

