stafford -- computes 2 generators for a given ideal in the Weyl algebra
***********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        stafford I
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, of the Weyl algebra
  * Outputs:
      * an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, with 2 generators (that has the
        same extension as I in $k(x)\langle dx\rangle)$

Description
===========

A theorem of Stafford says that every ideal in the Weyl algebra can be
 The current implementation provides a weaker result: the 2 generators
generated by 2 elements. This routine is the implementation of the effective
produced are guaranteed to generate only the extension of the ideal I in the
version of this theorem following the constructive proof in A.Leykin,
Weyl algebra with rational-function coefficients.
`Algorithmic proofs of two theorems of Stafford', Journal of Symbolic
Computation, 38(6):1535-1550, 2004.

+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : makeWA(QQ[x_1..x_4])                                |
|                                                         |
|o1 = QQ[x ..x , dx ..dx ]                                |
|         1   4    1    4                                 |
|                                                         |
