makeCyclic -- finds a cyclic generator of a D-module
****************************************************

  * Usage: 
        makeCyclic M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, that specifies a map such
        that coker M is a holonomic D-module
  * Outputs:
      * H, a *note hash table: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable,, where H.Generator is a
        cyclic generator and H.AnnG is the annihilator ideal of this generator

Description
===========

It is known that every holonomic module is cyclic and there is an algorithm for
computing a cyclic generator.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : makeWA(QQ[x])                                               |
|                                                                 |
|o1 = QQ[x, dx]                                                   |
|                                                                 |
|o1 : PolynomialRing, 1 differential variable(s)                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : M = matrix {{dx,0,0},{0,dx,0},{0,0,dx}} -- coker M = QQ[x]^3|
|                                                                 |
|o2 = | dx 0  0  |                                                |
|     | 0  dx 0  |                                                |
|     | 0  0  dx |                                                |
|                                                                 |
|                       3                3                        |
|o2 : Matrix (QQ[x, dx])  <-- (QQ[x, dx])                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : h = makeCyclic M                                            |
|                                                                 |
|                               3                                 |
|o3 = HashTable{AnnG => ideal dx   }                              |
|               Generator => | x2 |                               |
|                            | x  |                               |
|                            | 1  |                               |
|                                                                 |
|o3 : HashTable                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

The module M must be holonomic.

See also
========

  * *note isHolonomic: isHolonomic, -- determines whether a D-module (or ideal
    in Weyl algebra) is holonomic

